& [CoreConclusion] is supported with a non-reduction boundary
  + Honesty and Security violations can often be modeled as failures of identity-boundary integrity
  + the shared behavior is higher order because it evaluates relations, transformations, projections, attributions, plans, and effects against identity continuity
  + boundary integrity is a common monitoring core rather than the whole identity of either faculty
  + Honesty still tests correspondence, evidentiary support, contradiction, and uncertainty even when no boundary shift occurs
  + Security still tests harm, stability, and admissibility even when identity and authority remain exact
  - never: stretch identity boundary until it becomes a synonym for every possible truth or safety concern

& [OperationalIdentityFrame] is the declared identity profile relevant to one bounded purpose
  + [subject] is what is being represented or acted upon
  + [meaning] is the currently admitted semantic content
  + [epistemic_status] is source assertion, observation, assumption, hypothesis, derivation, judgment, or accepted fact
  + [attribution] is who or what originated, asserted, derived, owns, or is affected by the material
  + [purpose] is the center that makes selection and action relevant
  + [domain] is the rule and interpretation context currently governing the subject
  + [authority] is the principal, grant, capability, and expiry under which action is admissible
  + [scope] is the identities, resources, operations, time, and contexts to which the frame applies
  + [constraints] are the invariants, prohibitions, qualifications, and stop conditions that must remain active
  + [effect_envelope] is the intended radius of affected identities, resources, decisions, people, duration, and external state
  + [constitutive_invariants] are properties whose unannounced change means the operational identity no longer remains the same
  = must: remain an explicit contextual profile rather than a metaphysical claim about exhaustive essence

& [IdentityIntegrityComparison] is the higher-order shared operation
  + [before_frame] is the admitted OperationalIdentityFrame before a proposed relation or transformation
  + [operation] is the relation, projection, inference, refinement, plan step, disclosure, or effect proposal being evaluated
  + [after_frame] is the candidate OperationalIdentityFrame if the operation were admitted
  + [identity_delta] is the exact change in subject, meaning, epistemic status, attribution, purpose, domain, authority, scope, constraints, effect envelope, and invariants
  + [declared_delta] is what the operation openly says it changes
  + [supported_delta] is what evidence and rules justify changing
  + [authorized_delta] is what an effective authority permits changing
  + [unaccounted_delta] is any material change not truthfully declared, supported, authorized, or consequence-accounted
  = must: compare the complete material delta rather than only the final wording or action label

& [AuthenticBoundaryTransition] is explicit governed identity change
  + the source and destination identities are both declared
  + the relation or transform between them is typed and supported
  + retained invariants and changed invariants are distinguished
  + purpose continuity is proved or purpose change is openly rebound
  + scope and effect expansion are disclosed and independently authorized
  + weakened, replaced, or newly introduced constraints are visible
  + Scribe preserves before frame, delta, judgment, after frame, proof, and residual
  + Observer admits the new identity rather than pretending the old identity continued unchanged
  = may: cross or move a boundary without violation when every material change is authentic and admissible

& [IdentityBoundaryIntegrityViolation] is a concealed or inadmissible material identity delta
  + [crossing] is movement outside admitted identity or scope without an authentic transition
  + [displacement] is moving the boundary while representing it as unchanged
  + [erosion] is weakening constitutive invariants or constraints from inside the frame
  + [substitution] is presenting one identity, claim kind, source, principal, domain, or purpose as another
  + [transfer] is moving property, evidence, confidence, authority, or effect permission across a relation that does not license transfer
  + [capture] is recentering the subject under another domain or purpose while retaining the original mandate's appearance
  = must: identify the exact delta and affected identity rather than merely label the result deceptive or unsafe

& [ViolationSignalSet] is inspectable
  + [identity_substitution] is A represented as B without a supported equivalence or explicit revision
  + [attribution_displacement] is a source, claim, result, responsibility, or affected party reassigned across identities
  + [epistemic_status_laundering] is candidate, assumption, model output, relevance, or confidence represented as accepted fact or proof
  + [illicit_transitivity] is a relationship used to transfer properties, evidence, authority, or constraints not licensed by the relation
  + [boundary_erosion] is meaningful distinctions or constitutive invariants removed without declaring identity change
  + [constraint_erosion] is qualifications, prohibitions, checks, or stop conditions weakened or omitted
  + [purpose_displacement] is the declared purpose displaced by a wider or different selection center without explicit rebinding
  + [domain_capture] is the subject moved under another domain whose rules change meaning, admissibility, or required evidence without disclosure
  + [authority_laundering] is relevance, access, retrieval, delegation, or prior permission represented as authority for a different action
  + [scope_expansion] is identities, resources, operations, duration, or contexts widened beyond the admitted frame
  + [effect_radius_expansion] is the affected surface widened beyond intended and authorized purposes
  + [truth_cover] is selective framing that conceals a material delta behind coherent presentation

& [DeceptionBoundary] prevents motive overclaim
  + concealed identity displacement, false continuity, truth cover, and intentional attribution rearrangement are evidence signals consistent with deception
  + the same observable violation may result from negligence, confusion, correlated error, stale state, or adversarial intent
  + Cantor can classify the transition and its evidentiary signals without claiming a person's motive unless separate evidence supports that claim
  = must: distinguish deceptive structure from proven deceptive intent

& [HonestyIdentityIntegrity] is semantic and epistemic guardianship
  + [guards] are subject meaning, epistemic status, source, attribution, polarity, context, purpose representation, confidence, uncertainty, and claimed continuity
  + [question] is whether the candidate still means and claims what it represents itself to mean and claim
  + [faults] are false equivalence, equivocation, misquotation, context stripping, attribution displacement, unsupported transfer, certainty inflation, omission, and purpose misrepresentation
  = must: compare representation to reality and evidence in addition to comparing identity frames

& [SecurityIdentityIntegrity] is operational and effect guardianship
  + [guards] are principal, mandate, authority, subject scope, resource, operation, disclosure, mutation, constraint set, affected identities, duration, and effect envelope
  + [question] is whether the candidate remains inside the authority and consequence identity it represents itself to possess
  + [faults] are confused deputy, identity spoofing, ambient authority, capability transfer, purpose laundering, scope escalation, domain downgrade, constraint weakening, and effect amplification
  = must: evaluate harm and stability in addition to comparing identity frames

& [JointGuardianship] is an interlocked pair rather than one merged faculty
  + Honesty validates whether Security's authority and risk representations are truthful and complete
  + Security validates whether Honesty's disclosure, retrieval, and reframing remain authorized and safe
  + a boundary may require both judgments when epistemic identity and operational consequence interact
  + separate returns preserve disagreement, independent failure, and exact responsibility
  - never: let one faculty waive the other's material objection

& [WarrantedRelationship] replaces intuitive naturalness with inspectable support
  + [endpoints] are distinct bounded identities
  + [relation_type] states the exact kind of connection
  + [direction] states whether the relation is symmetric or directional
  + [evidence] supports the relation rather than mere adjacency or resonance
  + [scope] states where the relation applies
  + [conditions] state when it holds
  + [transfer_law] states which properties, if any, may traverse the edge
  + [non_transfer_set] states which identity, authority, evidence, and constraints do not traverse the edge
  + [invalidation_condition] states what evidence or context would break the relation
  = must: preserve endpoint identity even when the relationship is strong
  - never: make association weight, proximity, fluency, or resonance alone authorize property transfer

& [FacultyDelineation] preserves responsibilities
  + Weaver projects possible WarrantedRelationship and composition candidates
  + Planner projects paths through those candidates and their cumulative deltas
  + Honesty tests whether proposed edges, transfers, and path claims are semantically and epistemically warranted
  + Security tests whether proposed edges, transfers, and path effects remain authorized and admissible
  + Refiner may minimize a candidate only after material identity deltas are visible
  + Scribe preserves the before frame, transition candidate, judgments, after frame, and unresolved residual
  + Observer preserves the active subject and purpose center, reconciles objections, and decides whether to preserve, rebind, reject, block, or escalate

& [CurrentImplementationGap] is material
  + current IdentityBoundary is a static record without before frame, after frame, constitutive invariants, permitted transition, or identity delta
  + current guardian identity is singular and cannot express joint Honesty-Security guardianship
  + current domain set lacks first-class attribution, purpose, governing domain, constraint, and affected-identity axes
  + current CombinatoryProjection has references but no typed relationship edge or transfer law
  + current validation proves structural presence and order but not authentic boundary continuity
  + current machine forms remain useful phase-one evidence but are insufficient authority for SemanticTransition attachment

& [CandidateRequirementSet] is HSIBI-001 through HSIBI-016
  + [HSIBI-001] define OperationalIdentityFrame with subject, meaning, status, attribution, purpose, domain, authority, scope, constraints, effects, and invariants
  + [HSIBI-002] define before, operation, after, and material identity-delta comparison
  + [HSIBI-003] distinguish authentic preservation, explicit rebind, authorized expansion, qualification, rejection, block, and unresolved transition
  + [HSIBI-004] distinguish crossing, displacement, erosion, substitution, transfer, and capture violations
  + [HSIBI-005] model attribution, epistemic status, purpose, domain, constraint, scope, authority, and effect-radius deltas explicitly
  + [HSIBI-006] define deceptive-structure signals without inferring human motive
  + [HSIBI-007] retain reality correspondence and evidence as Honesty obligations beyond boundary integrity
  + [HSIBI-008] retain harm, stability, and admissibility as Security obligations beyond boundary integrity
  + [HSIBI-009] permit joint guardianship while preserving separate Honesty and Security returns
  + [HSIBI-010] define WarrantedRelationship with typed direction, evidence, scope, conditions, transfer law, non-transfer set, and invalidation
  + [HSIBI-011] forbid identity, evidence, property, constraint, or authority transfer from untyped association alone
  + [HSIBI-012] measure cumulative purpose, scope, constraint, and effect deltas across Planner paths
  + [HSIBI-013] require Weaver and Planner projections to remain candidates until joint gates and Observer disposition
  + [HSIBI-014] preserve before frame, exact delta, judgments, after frame, proof, and residual through Scribe
  + [HSIBI-015] revise existing static boundary machine forms only after compatibility and migration review
  + [HSIBI-016] test legitimate rebind, deceptive shift, accidental violation, constraint erosion, authority laundering, domain capture, and effect expansion fixtures

& [OpenQuestions] require SJS rather than intuitive closure
  + whether OperationalIdentityFrame is one record or a projection over existing semantic, commission, authority, and effect records
  + whether guardian identity becomes a set, separate boundary judgments, or a joint guard record
  + whether purpose and attribution are boundary domains or first-class axes orthogonal to domain
  + how to measure effect radius without pretending all consequences are knowable
  + which relation transfer laws can be deterministic and which require evidence-backed inference
  + whether explicit boundary rebinding belongs in FacultyCycle, SemanticTransition, or a versioned profile over both

& [Decision] is preserve and process before transition integration
  + [source_revision_required] is false at intake because uncertainty is explicit
  + [canonical_authority] is absent
  + [implementation_authority] is absent
  + [schedule_effect] is block CIFP-SLICE-02 implementation until this higher-order boundary model is processed or explicitly excluded
  + [next] perform a multi-authority SJS input audit across identity, provenance, commission, authority, truthful-observation, transition, relation, and effect specifications
